    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2051360751684591931",
      "url": "https://x.com/CXL_LAB/status/2051360751684591931",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/CXL_LAB/status/2051360751684591931",
      "text": "#Crypto Weekly News\n\n• StanChart + BlackRock + OKX launch BUIDL collateral framework\n• Securitize + CPU token-equities\n• Meta pays in USDC (Stripe)\n• Rayls launch\n• EigenCloud Acquisition\n• Polymarket + Chainalysis vs insiders\n• Trump “Project Freedom”\n\nNext:\n• HederaCon 2026 May 4\n• Consensus Miami May 5-7\n• ETHPrague May 8-10\n\nBUIDL collateral framework\nStandard Chartered, BlackRock, and OKX launched a framework letting OKX’s institutional clients use BlackRock’s BUIDL tokenized U.S. Treasury fund as yield-bearing collateral for trading, lending, and borrowing. Assets stay in regulated off-exchange custody at Standard Chartered (the first time a G-SIB has enabled this) bridging TradFi liquidity straight into crypto markets.\n\nSecuritize + CPU token-equities\nSecuritize teamed with Computershare to let U.S.-listed companies issue tokenized equities as Issuer-Sponsored Tokens (ISTs) alongside traditional shares. This opens a compliant on-chain path for the $70T U.S. stock market without changing existing market structure.\n\nMeta pays in USDC (Stripe)\nMeta began paying select creators directly in USDC via Stripe on Solana and Polygon blockchains. The rollout started in Colombia and the Philippines, letting users receive earnings straight to wallets like MetaMask or Phantom and skip traditional cross-border fees and delays.\n\nRayls launch\nRayls officially launched its public mainnet on April 30 (an EVM Layer-1 built for banks and institutions). It delivers enterprise-grade speed, tokenized real-world yield, and direct on-chain liquidity rails for regulated finance.\n\nEigenCloud Acquisition\nNebius agreed to acquire Eigen AI (strengthening its EigenCloud infrastructure) for ~$643M to boost AI inference and model optimization. The deal supercharges decentralized cloud capacity for Ethereum scaling and high-performance blockchain apps.\n\nPolymarket + Chainalysis vs insiders\nPolymarket partnered with Chainalysis to deploy real-time on-chain monitoring that detects and blocks insider trading and market manipulation. The new surveillance tools bring Wall Street-level integrity to crypto prediction markets.\n\nTrump “Project Freedom”\nTrump announced “Project Freedom,” a U.S. military operation to escort neutral cargo ships through the Strait of Hormuz amid ongoing Iran tensions. The move triggered a risk-on rally that pushed Bitcoin above $80,000 while easing some oil-supply fears.\n\nWhat’s the biggest catalyst for crypto this week: “Project Freedom” or Clarity Act finally getting traction (pushing Circle +20% intraday)?\n\nYour thoughts 👇",
