      "quoted_tweet": {
        "type": "tweet",
        "id": "2048642109008195773",
        "url": "https://x.com/CXL_LAB/status/2048642109008195773",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/CXL_LAB/status/2048642109008195773",
        "text": "#Crypto Weekly News\n\n• Apple: ~26 fake wallets\n• 120+ firms push CLARITY Act\n• Litecoin 13-block reorg\n• NY sued Coinbase/Gemini\n• Stripe L1 “Tempo”\n• SEC “tokenization exemption”\n• Trump crypto event at Mar-a-Lago\n• BIS stablecoin rules\n• Binance AI Wallet\n\nNext:\n• BTC Conf Apr 27-29\n• MegaETH + Rayls mainnet Apr 30\n• SUI/EIGEN/OMNI/ENA unlocks May 1-2\n\nApple: ~26 fake wallets\nKaspersky uncovered 26 malicious “FakeWallet” apps in the Apple App Store (China region) that perfectly mimic MetaMask, Coinbase Wallet, Ledger, Trust Wallet, and others. They steal seed phrases and drain funds instantly. Apple is removing them now.\n\n120+ firms push CLARITY Act\nOver 120 crypto companies (Coinbase, Ripple, Kraken, Circle, a16z) sent a joint letter to the Senate Banking Committee demanding immediate markup on the CLARITY Act before the May deadline. The bill already passed the House and would create clear rules separating commodities from securities.\n\nLitecoin 13-block reorg\nLitecoin suffered a DoS attack exploiting a zero-day in its MWEB protocol, forcing a 13-block reorganization (32 minutes of chain history). The fix was deployed quickly with no major user losses. It highlights ongoing risks for layer-1 upgrades and bridges.\n\nNY sued Coinbase/Gemini\nNew York AG Letitia James sued Coinbase and Gemini, claiming their prediction-market platforms are unlicensed illegal gambling operations. The suits seek injunctions and potentially billions in fines. This is a major test case for the multi-billion-dollar prediction market sector.\n\nStripe L1 “Tempo”\nStripe (with Paradigm) launched Tempo. It’s dedicated payments Layer-1. It introduces the Machine Payments Protocol so AI agents can autonomously pay across any rail. Public RPCs are now open for developers. DoorDash already using it.\n\nSEC “tokenization exemption”\nThe SEC confirmed tokenized real-world assets are still securities but introduced a new innovation exemption/sandbox for 2026. Eligible projects get temporary relief and lighter registration, speeding up institutional RWA adoption.\n\nTrump crypto event at Mar-a-Lago\nPresident Trump hosted an exclusive crypto conference at Mar-a-Lago for the top 297 holders of his TRUMP meme coin (top 29 got private access). The event mixed industry talks with personal branding and politics.\n\nBIS stablecoin rules\nThe Bank for International Settlements called for global coordination on stablecoin regulation to prevent fragmentation, runs, monetary-policy erosion, and risks to developing economies. Stablecoins are now too large for patchwork national rules.\n\nBinance AI Wallet\nBinance launched its Agentic AI Wallet. A keyless sub-account where AI agents can autonomously trade and manage assets within user-set limits. It’s designed to make DeFi safe and easy for non-technical users.\n\nWhich story do you think will have the biggest impact this week: Clarity Act, SEC exemption or Binance AI Agentic Wallet?\n\nShare your thoughts below 👇",
